# BOOT WITH ADDON of a 4 MB game with RESET on, the cart's ROM copy taking
# 128 frames (OMEGA_COPY_RATE, 32 KB a frame), as boot-copy does for CLEAN
# BOOT: the addon launch's own copy path, with the bar moved by the VBlank
# estimate (source/progress.h) while the cart copies. The game's IRQ hook
# comes from its PATCH/ file (as on a second launch, made by one launch of
# this game: tests/shots/data/addon-copy.pat), so the cart copies the ROM
# before the kernel patches it; a first launch scans the ROM instead. Its
# first frames are hashed, and every frame of the copy is watched for tears. The launch goes
# through the menu's test hook (tests/nav.sh).
#! settings 1=1
#! sd-file "/Big Adventure (Europe).gba" 0x400000 tests/roms/hello/hello.gba
#! sd-file "/PATCH/Big Adventure (Europe).pat" 0 tests/shots/data/addon-copy.pat
#! env OMEGA_COPY_RATE=0x8000
-w "nav: home ready"
-P "@8:nav_test_path:/Big Adventure (Europe).gba" -p @8:nav_test_action:0x7E000002
-w "BOOT WITH ADDON: reset 1"
-H @6:@12
-T @1:@130
-s @40:fast.png
-s @110:slow.png
-w "launch: the cart copied"
-s @0:copied.png
